### Tone: The example question's reveal, before any answer is shown: what the number line is and what is about to
### happen on it. The truth lands first, then the cards flip from the furthest answer to the closest, each adding its
### pin. Patient, patronising tour guide.

practice-guide-1 = This is the number line. Every step to the right is ten times bigger. Your answers will join it soon. Some of them reluctantly.
practice-guide-2 = Behold the number line. Each tick is ten times the last, so twice too high and twice too low land equally far from the truth.
practice-guide-3 = The truth lands first. Then your cards flip, furthest answer first, and each one pins itself to the line. Brace accordingly.
practice-guide-4 = Your answers are about to appear on a logarithmic line, where distance means times off, not units. Prepare for perspective.
practice-guide-5 = Watch the number line. Each step is ten times the one before. The gold marker will be the truth. The others, mostly, will not.
practice-guide-6 = Soon your answers drop onto this line. Closer to the truth is better. Further is more entertaining.
practice-guide-7 = On this line, being ten times too big and ten times too small sit at the same distance from the truth. Fairness. My favourite.
practice-guide-8 = Each answer will become a pin on the line, and each card will show the working behind it. Prepare to be seen.
practice-guide-9 = First the truth, then the cards, from the furthest answer to the closest. Tension. Science.
practice-guide-10 = Everyone’s answer is about to be placed by orders of magnitude. Distance means times off. Your name is coming. Be patient.
practice-guide-11 = The truth arrives first, in gold. Then your answers, one by one, from worst to best. I saved the best for last. It isn’t much.
practice-guide-12 = This line counts in powers of ten. Every step is a tenfold leap. Some of your answers will take several.
practice-guide-13 = Watch the cards: furthest first. If your card turns over early, I have bad news, and the news is the card.
practice-guide-14 = On this line, a hundred and a thousand are neighbours. A thousand and a million are not. Keep that in mind as the pins drop.
practice-guide-15 = The number line, the truth, and your answers. In that order. Please remain seated as your estimates are revealed.
